      "status": 200
    },
    {
      "path": "/v1/realtime/calls",
      "status": 201
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "content": "The Sound collection includes these directly relevant studies:\n\n- **2005 — “Recreational music-making modulates the human stress response: a preliminary individualized gene expression strategy.”** Reported reversal of stress-induced gene-expression signatures. **IL6** changes occurred in both the music-making and resting-control groups, so that finding was not unique to music-making. [S1]\n\n- **2007 — “Recreational music-making modulates natural killer cell activity, cytokines, and mood states in corporate employees.”** Reported gene-expression changes involving **interferon-gamma and interleukin-10**, alongside improved mood. The retrieved record does not specify the direction or magnitude of those expression changes. [S2]\n\n- **2013 — “Recreational Music-Making alters gene expression pathways in patients with coronary heart disease.”** Reported gene-expression pathway changes; the authors suggested active music-making may alter expression more effectively than quiet reading. The approved record does not identify individual genes or effect sizes. [S3]\n\nAll appeared in *Medical Science Monitor*. These are specifically recreational music-making studies, rather than listening-only or professional-performance studies.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "id": "pmid-15668624",
        "title": "Recreational music-making modulates the human stress response: a preliminary individualized gene expression strategy",
        "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15668624/"
      },
      {
        "id": "pmid-17261984",
        "title": "Recreational music-making modulates natural killer cell activity, cytokines, and mood states in corporate employees",
        "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17261984/"
      },
      {
        "id": "pmid-23435350",
        "title": "Recreational Music-Making alters gene expression pathways in patients with coronary heart disease",
        "url": "https://doi.org/10.12659/msm.883807"
      }
    ]
  },
